      "type": "text",
      "text": "All electives must be upper-division courses in engineering. Technical elective (TE) course selections must have departmental approval prior to taking the courses."
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Two consecutive quarters of independent research (CENG 199) can be approved as equivalent to two technical elective courses (eight units)."
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Students are allowed to take one of the following four-unit 'Teams in Engineering Service' courses: ENG 100D or ENG 100B and ENG 100L or two quarters of ENG 100L as an approved Engineering Focus elective."
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Any other upper-division course in engineering, with departmental approval"
     }
    ],
    "units": 12,
    "label": "Technical Electives",
    "notes": "Electives are intended to broaden and enhance professional goals. All electives must be upper-division courses in engineering. Suggestions are listed by area in the catalog. Courses such as CENG 195, 197, and 198 are not allowed as a technical elective. CENG 199 can be used as a technical elective only under restrictive conditions. NANO 156 and MAE 166 are cross-listed; CENG majors must enroll in NANO 156."
   }
