 ],
 "narrative": [
  "To graduate, students must maintain an overall GPA of at least 2.0.",
  "Every course required for the major (except CENG 4 and CENG 199) must be taken for a letter grade, including all CENG and technical elective courses. This also includes all MATH, BILD, CHEM, and PHYS courses. All major requirements must have a grade of C- or higher.",
  "The chemical engineering major is a selective major. Only students who have completed the required screening courses and have a minimum 2.0 UC GPA are eligible to apply.",
  "Screening courses (first-year applicants): MATH 20A, 20B, 20C, PHYS 2A, 2B, CHEM 6A, 6B, 6C, 7L. Screening courses (second-year applicants): MATH 20A, 20B, 20C, 20D, MATH 18, PHYS 2A, 2B, 2C, 2CL, CHEM 6A, 6B, 6C, 7L.",
  "All transfer students must take CENG 4 and CENG 15 (MATLAB) in the fall or winter of their first year at UC San Diego.",
  "NANO 156 and MAE 166 are cross-listed courses; CENG majors must enroll in NANO 156. NANO 175 and CENG 175 are cross-listed courses and credit cannot be given for both."
 ]
